The agent record of the Android chat view, an ngterm extension: the adapters that own the four events the record
needs pipe the hook payload to `ngtermctl agent hook <claude|codex> <event>`, which parses it in Rust and sends
`agent.report`. Claude Code's SessionStart and SessionEnd go through the restore adapter, under its guards (the
interactive CLI only, no subagent), every end whatever its reason; its UserPromptSubmit and PermissionRequest through
the Claude status adapter, which reads the payload's head for the event an `active` or `blocked` call stands for (so a
PostToolUse payload stays unread), after its process-topology walk and only for the interactive CLI, a subagent's
prompt left out. Codex's SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit and PermissionRequest go through its adapter, which reads
those three payloads once and hands them on to its own readers; a subagent's events other than a permission prompt are
left out. PostToolUse and Stop make no call. The PowerShell forms do the same, reading and handing on the payload as
UTF-8. Applied after 0005-codex-own-process.patch.

